   133	    // Drag-only, subiter-invariant wake signal (KTD-9): the grain's local relative flow speed
   134	    // |mean(v_water) − v_grain|, computed once per substep BEFORE the Jacobi drag subiters — so it is
   135	    // independent of dt / subiter count and never carries a buoyancy contribution (a hydrostatic,
   136	    // zero-flow saturated bed reads ≈0 and stays asleep). finalize consults it to keep a grain in
   137	    // moving water awake. Recomputed every substep, so it needs no explicit decay: when the flow
   138	    // stops it drops to ≈0 on its own and the grain re-sleeps.
   139	    if (ph_i == PHASE_GRAIN && n > 0.0) {
